#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Integral of a Logarithmic Expression Using Integration by Parts Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f53230a-ac18-5819-b7aa-8fc4cd6a24fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(3{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290209} {:answer/id #uuid "04d9df7e-0377-57d5-8cae-d60a0dc50cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290210} {:answer/id #uuid "2cea4065-d7d7-58a4-a77e-122972c73e74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290211} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa58726-c13b-5add-834b-ac023e4a62ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{3{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290212} {:answer/id #uuid "68ec665d-5383-56a5-8aec-69399e614220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68ec665d-5383-56a5-8aec-69399e614220" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290213} :answer-field/id #uuid "044cf0d4-63f0-5c69-ba32-5a850ebc7d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35c6bb4e-1ad8-5bd0-8b19-4423d0943b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-12708" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$"}]}
